WEBVTT

00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:00.750
where people ask you about your hobbies,

00:08:00.774 --> 00:08:02.702
and if you were stuck on a desert island

00:08:02.726 --> 00:08:04.892
and you could only pick
three people on earth,

00:08:04.916 --> 00:08:06.137
what would you do?

00:08:06.161 --> 00:08:07.557
Why do you want to work here?

00:08:07.581 --> 00:08:08.827
And we know from research,

00:08:08.851 --> 00:08:12.365
those are some of the worst predictors
of job performance you can have.

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:14.113
AG: Lauren Rivera is a sociologist

00:08:14.137 --> 00:08:16.402
at Northwestern's Kellogg
School of Management

00:08:16.426 --> 00:08:19.134
and one of the world's
leading experts on hiring.

00:08:19.158 --> 00:08:22.660
Lauren first got interested in the topic
when she was a senior in college,

00:08:22.684 --> 00:08:25.430
and she went to interview
for a management consulting job.

00:08:25.454 --> 00:08:27.470
LR: It was a high-stakes interview for me.

00:08:27.494 --> 00:08:29.946
You know, I supported my family
all through college,

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.599
paid the rent and stuff like that.